WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.400
-Jimmie, you were a NASCAR
driver for 20 years?

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.100
-Yeah, basically.
-Yeah, and -- and retired.

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:07.467
-That's a funny word.

00:00:07.467 --> 00:00:08.534
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:08.534 --> 00:00:10.133
But I mean, what --
what happened,

00:00:10.133 --> 00:00:13.934
and what's the difference
between NASCAR and Indy?

00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:16.367
-The car performance
of the Indy car is probably

00:00:16.367 --> 00:00:18.467
two to three times
of what a NASCAR vehicle is.

00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:19.801
So, it's hard to believe that,

00:00:19.801 --> 00:00:22.100
just 'cause a NASCAR vehicle
is so fast.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:24.834
But these little sporty cars,
with the shape of the car,

00:00:24.834 --> 00:00:27.667
and the big tires on 'em, and
the speed, they're just a rush.

00:00:27.667 --> 00:00:30.834
And I truly thought
that I was going to slow down.

00:00:30.834 --> 00:00:32.767
And then I had a chance to drive
one of these Indy cars,

00:00:32.767 --> 00:00:34.334
and I thought, "Okay.
Well I'll just try

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:36.567
a limited schedule in '21."
And now I here --

00:00:36.567 --> 00:00:38.400
you know, here I am in '22
with a full schedule.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:41.367
-But I mean,
so what does your wife say?

00:00:41.367 --> 00:00:43.133
-Um, yeah, you know,
that's been a -- been a --

00:00:43.133 --> 00:00:44.367
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.367 --> 00:00:46.200
-She goes, "Wait, wait.
You were just out.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:47.234
Well, now you're
in the crazier thing."

00:00:47.234 --> 00:00:48.567
-"We're gonna slow down."

00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:50.067
And then it's honestly
been busier.

00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:53.334
And then the car is a bit more
dangerous and certainly faster.

00:00:53.334 --> 00:00:55.501
Yeah.
-How fast have you ever gone?

00:00:55.501 --> 00:00:58.934
-The fastest would be in this
car in qualifying last Sunday.

00:00:58.934 --> 00:01:01.801
It was over 240 miles an hour
entering turn 1.

00:01:01.801 --> 00:01:03.868
-Geez.
-The average speed for the lap,

00:01:03.868 --> 00:01:06.133
for the pole -- and my teammate,
Scott Dixon, won the pole --

00:01:06.133 --> 00:01:10.167
the average speed for four laps
was 234 miles an hour.

00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:12.200
-What do you see
when you're driving 204 --

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:14.567
[ Laughter ]
Like, what -- what do you do?

00:01:14.567 --> 00:01:16.167
Like, what --
-It's like "Star Wars"

00:01:16.167 --> 00:01:18.067
when they hit the gas
in the Millennium Falcon.

00:01:18.067 --> 00:01:19.601
-Yeah.
-That's -- That's it.

00:01:19.601 --> 00:01:22.868
-How do you know when to turn
or how to stay on anything?

00:01:22.868 --> 00:01:24.901
I mean --
-It's -- It's a rush.

00:01:24.901 --> 00:01:26.367
Yeah, there's a lot going on.
-Yeah.

00:01:26.367 --> 00:01:29.000
-It's -- It's so gnarly.
Like, that's been --

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:30.467
You know, the kid in me,
the racer in me,

00:01:30.467 --> 00:01:33.033
loves that experience.
And it's just been so cool.

00:01:33.033 --> 00:01:34.734
-How about
in your personal life, do --

00:01:34.734 --> 00:01:36.501
are you the driver
in the family, or...?

00:01:36.501 --> 00:01:38.334
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:38.334 --> 00:01:40.200
-Like, could I ask,
if I'm going out with you,

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.033
can I ask that your wife
drive us to this?

00:01:42.033 --> 00:01:43.868
[ Laughter ]
I don't want to go 220

00:01:43.868 --> 00:01:45.033
to the mall, I mean --

00:01:45.033 --> 00:01:47.367
-It would be a safer option
for two reasons.

00:01:47.367 --> 00:01:49.501
One, you know,
there's less risk,

00:01:49.501 --> 00:01:51.968
and, two, you wouldn't have
any vomit in the car.

00:01:51.968 --> 00:01:54.000
[ Audience groans ]
I get motion sickness so bad.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.234
-You do?
-I do.

00:01:55.234 --> 00:01:56.534
-Wait. What?
-I do.

00:01:56.534 --> 00:01:58.234
-But that --
How is that possible?

00:01:58.234 --> 00:01:59.968
-It is.
I don't -- I don't know.

00:01:59.968 --> 00:02:01.501
-Do you get sick
while you're racing?

00:02:01.501 --> 00:02:04.434
-Not while I'm driving, but
riding in a car, it's horrible.

00:02:04.434 --> 00:02:06.167
-Wow.
-Taxi cabs, those guys?

00:02:06.167 --> 00:02:07.334
-Well, yeah, okay,
I'll give it to you, yeah.

00:02:07.334 --> 00:02:08.367
I'll give it to you,
that's very -- yeah.

00:02:08.367 --> 00:02:09.501
-I mean...

00:02:09.501 --> 00:02:11.133
-But your whole family's
involved.

00:02:11.133 --> 00:02:13.200
I know that your dad
is part of your crew.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:15.167
-He is this year, yeah.
-He's one of your --

00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:16.834
-He's been with me forever,
throughout racing,

00:02:16.834 --> 00:02:18.968
got me started.
But he's a crew member

00:02:18.968 --> 00:02:20.868
on the race car
for the Indianapolis 500.

00:02:20.868 --> 00:02:22.367
-So he's supportive, as well.
-Yeah.

00:02:22.367 --> 00:02:24.100
Yeah, he's gonna be spotting
for me -- the guys that --

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:26.000
I have two guys, one on each end
of the speedway,

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.634
that tell me where other cars
are around me,

00:02:27.634 --> 00:02:29.033
kind of spot
the dangerous parts.

00:02:29.033 --> 00:02:31.100
-But how --
if you're going that fast,

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:33.968
how can you tell who's what,
and where anyone is, and --

00:02:33.968 --> 00:02:35.067
that fast?

00:02:35.067 --> 00:02:36.968
Does your dad talk like an
auctioneer?

00:02:36.968 --> 00:02:38.100
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:40.801
Like --
[ Mimicking auctioneer ]

00:02:40.801 --> 00:02:42.567
-While looking
through binoculars.

00:02:42.567 --> 00:02:43.701
-Does -- yeah, I mean.

00:02:43.701 --> 00:02:45.367
Binoculars,
I feel like that's useless.

00:02:45.367 --> 00:02:46.667
-But that's how they do it.

00:02:46.667 --> 00:02:48.801
-But how could you
even go that fast?

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:51.334
-I tried it once for my younger
brother when he was racing,

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:52.801
and he was just yelling at me
the whole time

00:02:52.801 --> 00:02:53.968
because I was looking
at the wrong car

00:02:53.968 --> 00:02:55.901
and giving the wrong commands.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.901 --> 00:02:59.200
It's a -- It's a specialized
form of work.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:01.167
-Well, I know
that you're not the --

00:03:01.167 --> 00:03:03.367
he's not the only family member
helping you out on the track.

00:03:03.367 --> 00:03:05.133
Because you're recovering
from a hand injury.

00:03:05.133 --> 00:03:07.133
-Yes.
-And your daughter was out there

00:03:07.133 --> 00:03:09.234
to give you a pep talk.
And we have a video.

00:03:09.234 --> 00:03:10.601
This is very cute.
Take a look at this.

00:03:10.601 --> 00:03:11.634
-Have fun.

00:03:17.901 --> 00:03:19.400
-Thanks, baby.

00:03:20.634 --> 00:03:22.601
[ Laughter ]
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:26.100
-That's Lydia, my wife Chandra,
and then our oldest, Genevieve,

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.400
was off on the side there.

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:28.701
But Lydia gave me
some great advice.

00:03:28.701 --> 00:03:30.100
-What were you thinking there
when she was like,

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:33.033
"Yeah, no matter where you
place, you just -- you tried."

00:03:33.033 --> 00:03:34.968
-I was very happy to hear it,
but in my mind,

00:03:34.968 --> 00:03:37.000
I'm like, "I'm a pro athlete.
I've gotta win.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.367
I've gotta place."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.367 --> 00:03:40.167
-Like, "Honey, I'll talk to you
after the race," yeah.

00:03:40.167 --> 00:03:42.067
-"10 years from now,
we'll talk about this."

00:03:42.067 --> 00:03:44.968
-You decided to customize
your helmet

00:03:44.968 --> 00:03:47.267
that you're going to wear
for your first Indy 500.

00:03:47.267 --> 00:03:48.868
-Yes.
-And you got to design it

00:03:48.868 --> 00:03:50.534
with Blake Shelton.
-I did.

00:03:50.534 --> 00:03:53.667
-How did you get involved
with that -- with that man.

00:03:53.667 --> 00:03:54.968
-That man.
-That animal.

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:57.367
-That animal.
-That beast, Blake Shelton.

00:03:57.367 --> 00:03:59.567
-Well, at this point
in my career and life,

00:03:59.567 --> 00:04:01.667
I just want to do fun things
with friends.

00:04:01.667 --> 00:04:04.834
And to have this opportunity
to design a helmet together,

00:04:04.834 --> 00:04:06.968
you know, was something
that I couldn't pass up.

00:04:06.968 --> 00:04:08.767
We're supporting
the American Legion.

00:04:08.767 --> 00:04:10.534
It's Memorial Day weekend.

00:04:10.534 --> 00:04:13.400
Blake's family served,
my grandfather served,

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:15.734
so we've created a helmet --
and really, you'll --

00:04:15.734 --> 00:04:17.334
you'll appreciate this a lot.

00:04:17.334 --> 00:04:20.868
Blake wanted to sew a mullet
into the back of the helmet.

00:04:20.868 --> 00:04:22.934
That was like the one thing that
he really wanted in the design.

00:04:22.934 --> 00:04:24.367
-Oh, my gosh, Blake.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.367 --> 00:04:26.567
Thank goodness you didn't --
not do that.

00:04:26.567 --> 00:04:27.868
-Well --
-You thought about it?

00:04:27.868 --> 00:04:29.834
-He'll be there Sunday,
so we'll see what happens.

00:04:29.834 --> 00:04:31.334
-He wanted to put a mullet
in your helmet?

00:04:31.334 --> 00:04:32.567
-He was like,
"Man, that'd be so cool."

00:04:32.567 --> 00:04:33.701
[ Laughter ]
"We just put a mullet

00:04:33.701 --> 00:04:36.234
in the back,
and you put your helmet on."

00:04:36.234 --> 00:04:39.133
-I'm -- what did you --
what did you end up going with?

00:04:39.133 --> 00:04:41.834
-We -- Troy Lee Designs
designed the helmet,

00:04:41.834 --> 00:04:44.634
and we came up with a really
cool, you know,

00:04:44.634 --> 00:04:46.901
patriotic helmet that has some
jets on the top

00:04:46.901 --> 00:04:48.033
and our grandfathers --

00:04:48.033 --> 00:04:49.634
our family members
that are on the side.

00:04:49.634 --> 00:04:53.334
-Yeah, I want to -- I want to
bring -- show you the helmet.

00:04:53.334 --> 00:04:54.801
You brought it with you tonight.
-We do.

00:04:54.801 --> 00:04:58.834
-But even more special, someone
is going to bring out the helmet

00:04:58.834 --> 00:05:01.767
and deliver this to us,
so we can all take a look at it.

00:05:01.767 --> 00:05:04.734
Ladies and gentlemen,
please welcome Lydia.

00:05:04.734 --> 00:05:07.934
Lydia, are you there?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:07.934 --> 00:05:09.601
♪♪

00:05:09.601 --> 00:05:12.767
You can come over here.
How did you --

00:05:12.767 --> 00:05:14.200
-Thank you, sweetie.
-You are --

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:17.267
Lydia, you are so beautiful.

00:05:17.267 --> 00:05:20.067
And that was
a great video message

00:05:20.067 --> 00:05:21.434
I saw you did
with your dad there. Yeah.

00:05:21.434 --> 00:05:23.567
-[ Chuckles ]
-And I was talking

00:05:23.567 --> 00:05:26.167
to you backstage, and I said,
"If you'd like to come out

00:05:26.167 --> 00:05:28.367
while your dad's --
you can look from the crowd."

00:05:28.367 --> 00:05:30.801
And you go,
"Why can't I be on the show?"

00:05:30.801 --> 00:05:32.334
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.334 --> 00:05:34.334
And I go, "Well, of course
we can make that happen."

00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:37.467
And I just thought that was
so cute and funny of you.

00:05:37.467 --> 00:05:38.934
So, welcome
to "The Tonight Show."

00:05:38.934 --> 00:05:43.767
Does it feel good?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:43.767 --> 00:05:45.567
Here it is.
Oh, my God.

00:05:45.567 --> 00:05:47.033
Look at this.
Look at this, right here,

00:05:47.033 --> 00:05:48.501
ladies and gentlemen.
-Yes, my grandfather's here.

00:05:48.501 --> 00:05:50.601
These are Blake's --
one is Blake's brother,

00:05:50.601 --> 00:05:53.234
and the other is Blake's father.

00:05:53.234 --> 00:05:55.400
Memorial Day weekend,
honoring the men and women

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:57.200
that have paid
the ultimate sacrifice.

00:05:57.200 --> 00:05:59.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
With this helmet.

00:05:59.033 --> 00:06:01.200
-Best of luck this weekend.
I'm so happy.

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:03.000
Come back whenever, you know.
-Thank you so much.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.467
-Lydia, it's an honor
to have you here.

00:06:04.467 --> 00:06:06.000
Thank you so much, Lydia.
-Thank you.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:09.033
-Jimmie Johnson, everybody!
Coverage of the Indy 500

00:06:09.033 --> 00:06:12.467
starts live at 11:00 a.m.,
this Sunday, right here on NBC.

